{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "eval.2026-07-29-eval-202743.rag-ingestion-retrieval",
  "title": "RAG ingestion, retrieval, and index rebuild",
  "description": "# Retrieval-augmented generation: ingestion to grounded answers\n\nThis diagram follows knowledge left-to-right from scheduled or change-triggered source arrivals through normalization, version classification, chunking, embedding, and version-consistent publication to vector, document, and keyword stores. Unparseable content is quarantined; transient embedding failures retry and persistent failures enter a dead-letter store.\n\nThe serving path rewrites a user question, performs hybrid retrieval, fuses and reranks results, applies access controls, and either produces an evidence-grounded answer with citations or says it does not know when evidence is insufficient. Feedback identifies coverage gaps and feeds ingestion priorities.\n\nThe bottom lane shows embedding-model replacement: a coordinator re-embeds the corpus into a new index generation while live queries remain on the current generation, then promotes the complete generation atomically while retaining the prior generation for rollback.",
  "mode": "diagram",
  "viewport": {
    "x": 0,
    "y": 0,
    "zoom": 1
  },
